const esc=s=>String(s??'').replaceAll('|','\\|').replaceAll('\n',' ');
const table=(headers,data)=>'| '+headers.map(esc).join(' | ')+' |\n| '+headers.map(()=>'---').join(' | ')+' |\n'+data.map(r=>'| '+r.map(esc).join(' | ')+' |').join('\n');
const sourceLink=k=>`[${sources[k][0]}](${sources[k][1]})`;
const link=p=>`[${p}](${base+p})`;
const intro=`# MASTER KEYWORD-TO-URL MATRIX\n\n## Success Path Mentors — management approval report\n\n**Analysis only. No website, page, metadata, URL, navigation, schema, redirect, or location architecture changes were made.**\n\nDomain: ${base}. Live audit: ${crawl.summary.checkedAt}. Keyword market: primarily English-language parent/student acquisition; existing French-language program assessed in its own language. Arabic keyword research is not inferred from English keywords.\n\n## Executive recommendation\n\nPrioritize existing service hubs and the already-published curriculum pages. Approve one carefully scoped new cross-subject school-exam preparation page for a later implementation brief. Keep MCV4U, senior biology and language/specialist expansion on HOLD until actual delivery and unique materials are established. This report does not authorize implementation.\n\n${table(['Measure','Count'],[['Clusters reviewed',rows.length],['OPTIMIZE EXISTING',counts[O]],['CREATE NEW',counts[N]],['MERGE INTO ONE PAGE',counts[M]],['HOLD / DO NOT TARGET YET',counts[H]],['Distinct existing target URLs',existingOwners.length],['Candidate keyword phrases (deduplicated; no volume implied)',uniqueKeywords.size],['Live non-location pages audited',80],['Additional candidate routes checked (all 404)',9]])}\n\nCounts use one mutually exclusive decision per cluster, not one decision per spelling variant. MERGE means consolidating keyword ownership on one existing URL; it does **not** recommend merging/deleting pages or adding redirects.\n\n## 1. Current architecture and findings\n\nThe live sitemap supplied 80 English/French non-location URLs: 67 English and 13 French. All returned HTTP 200. These include four English legal utility pages, which were inventoried but excluded from acquisition targeting. No location pages were fetched. A source-only lookup records existing location ownership for HOLD rows.\n\n- ${link('/en')} is the broad tutoring owner. Programs, Services, Pricing and FAQ already exist as #programs, #services, #pricing and #faq. These fragments are sections of /en, not separately indexable pages.\n- ${link('/en/subjects')} is a directory, not a second generic math/science landing page. The six displayed areas comprise math, English, general science, chemistry, physics and the separate French program.\n- Five English main subject pages have 52 existing child pathways/strands: math 8, English 11, general science 4, chemistry 16, physics 13. Subject pages already support grade navigation; there are no separate grade URLs in the current sitemap.\n- Math currently states Grades 2–12; do not infer Grade 1 mathematics from the homepage's general Grades 1–12 offer. Chemistry's body identifies Grades 5 and 8–12, while its title summarizes Grades 5–12. This is a positioning/coverage check for management, not permission to rewrite anything.\n- Many child titles use “by Grade” and the body emphasizes curriculum inventories. The principal opportunity is to explain the specific tutoring problem and support process on those existing pages. Topic catalog presence alone does not prove full Ontario course alignment.\n- ${link('/fr/programme-francais')} is French and mathematics taught in French. Its subject/domain pages are real curriculum assets; they are not a French translation of the English homepage. English “French tutoring” demand remains a separate unresolved language/intent decision.\n- /en/programs, /en/services, /en/faq, /en/blog, /en/subjects/french, /en/subjects/biology, /en/subjects/science, /en/subjects/math/calculus-vectors and /en/subjects/math/mcv4u returned 404. These were diagnostic candidate checks, not a list of broken internal links and not a recommendation to create nine pages.\n\nCurrent titles, H1s, HTTP statuses and exact URLs for every audited page are in the inventory below and in crawl.json. Extraction includes Next.js streamed HTML nodes; no missing-H1 claim is based on the initial main-element placeholder.\n\n## 2. Evidence and decision rules\n\n- **Observed:** current SPM titles, H1s, main content, grade/topic organization, forms and sitemap. Titles are copied exactly into the matrix; a related existing page is identified for new/HOLD candidates.\n- **Inferred:** keyword wording, intent grouping, positioning, priority and potential cannibalization. These are management recommendations, not measured rankings or established traffic loss.\n- **DATA REQUIRED:** search volume, keyword difficulty, country/language-specific demand, Search Console query/page history, conversions and revenue by service. All rows explicitly leave volume and difficulty unestimated.\n- Competitor examples demonstrate current service/architecture patterns. Exact long-tail matches are labelled when not validated. Competitor publication alone does not justify copying its URL structure or adding an SPM service.\n- P1: core service conversion or urgent scope verification; P2: useful existing-page improvements or the distinct exam-service gap; P3: narrower candidates and deferred work. A P1 HOLD remains HOLD. Priorities are qualitative, not volume-based.\n- Funnel: TOFU = problem awareness, MOFU = comparison/evaluation, BOFU = inquiry/booking. Each row's primary keyword is the **target page's main owner**, so multiple grade/use-case rows can share it without assigning competing primary owners.\n\nCompetitor patterns used: ${sourceLink('oxSubjects')} and ${sourceLink('oxPrograms')} separate subject, skill and program browsing. ${sourceLink('evolveMath')}, ${sourceLink('evolveChem')} and ${sourceLink('evolvePhysics')} illustrate subject hubs that can accommodate school grades/course context. Evolve also publishes individual course pages (${sourceLink('mcr')}, ${sourceLink('mhf')}, ${sourceLink('mcv')}, ${sourceLink('mdm')}); this is evidence of distinct course vocabulary, not a requirement for SPM to create all four. ${sourceLink('math101')} demonstrates navigation by course code.\n\n## 3. Ontario terminology and boundaries\n\n${table(['Code','Official course name','Grade / stream','SPM decision'],[['MCR3U','Functions','11 / University Preparation','Existing Functions pathway; accurate course-support section'],['MHF4U','Advanced Functions','12 / University Preparation','Merge name/code variants into advanced-precalculus'],['MCV4U','Calculus and Vectors','12 / University Preparation','HOLD pending full service/materials confirmation'],['MDM4U','Mathematics of Data Management','12 / University Preparation','Merge into statistics-probability'],['MTH1W','Mathematics','9 / De-streamed','Support current Grade 9 context within math hub'],['SCH3U / SCH4U','Chemistry','11 / 12 University Preparation','Existing chemistry hub, separate grade/course sections'],['SPH3U / SPH4U','Physics','11 / 12 University Preparation','Existing physics hub, separate grade/course sections']])}\n\nNames and senior-course codes are grounded in ${sourceLink('ontMath')} and ${sourceLink('ontScience')}. The ministry's ${sourceLink('ontCurrent')} retains the senior math documents while identifying the current MTH1W course; ${sourceLink('ontGrade9')} independently confirms MTH1W in current policy. Historical MPM1D/MFM1P terms should not be presented as today's mainstream Grade 9 course. Grade 10 academic/applied streams are distinct. Grade 11/12 wording is broader than any one University Preparation code.\n\n**Course-code intent is not city intent.** MCR3U/MHF4U/MDM4U can be discussed accurately within non-location subject pages. Broad “Ontario online tutoring” and “Ontario curriculum tutoring” already overlap locked location/curriculum owners and remain HOLD. No recommendations are made to those owners.\n\n## 4. Master matrix\n\nEach row contains all requested fields. Full URLs are retained. For HOLD, the recommended target is deliberately unassigned; a related URL is context, not authorization to optimize it.\n\n`;
const headers=['ID','Keyword / cluster','Search intent','Funnel stage','Subject','Grade','Curriculum / course code','Existing URL / related page','Current title of existing page','Recommended target URL','Decision','Reason','Primary keyword (page owner)','Supporting keywords','Cannibalization risk','Competitor example','Competitor relevance','Priority','Search volume','Keyword difficulty'];
const matrixData=rows.map(r=>[r.id,r.keyword,r.searchIntent,r.funnel,r.subject,r.grade,r.course,r.existingUrl,r.currentTitle,r.targetUrl,r.decision,r.reason,r.primaryKeyword,r.supportingKeywords,r.cannibalizationRisk,r.competitorExample?`[${r.competitorExample[0]}](${r.competitorExample[1]})`:'None validated / not applicable',r.competitorScope,r.priority,r.volume,r.keywordDifficulty]);
const summaryA='\n\n## A. EXISTING PAGES TO OPTIMIZE\n\nOne row per existing target URL, including owners receiving MERGE clusters. These are recommendations for later approval, not drafted replacement copy.\n\n'+table(['URL','Primary keyword','Recommended positioning','Priority'],existingOwners.map(([p,o])=>[abs(p),o.primary,o.positioning,o.priority]));
const summaryB=`\n\n## B. NEW PAGES RECOMMENDED\n\n${table(['Proposed URL','Primary keyword','Intent','Reason new page is justified','Priority'],rows.filter(r=>r.decision===N).map(r=>[r.targetUrl,r.primaryKeyword,r.searchIntent,r.reason,r.priority]))}\n\n### Five-part threshold: school exam preparation\n\n1. **Distinct intent:** arrange focused preparation around a school assessment, rather than browse a subject curriculum or general tutoring package.\n2. **No adequate existing owner:** homepage coverage is a short service description; the existing assessment/test-preparation page is explicitly an English strand.\n3. **Unique educational value is feasible:** a diagnostic-to-revision process, example preparation timelines, subject-specific practice selection, error-review methods and realistic parent/student expectations. This describes a future brief, not newly authored lesson content.\n4. **Manageable overlap:** the new page owns generic cross-subject school-exam help only. Math/chemistry/physics exam questions stay supporting terms on their respective subject hubs; English assessment content stays on its existing strand.\n5. **Real service evidence:** the live homepage lists Exam Preparation and Focused Exam Preparation, with practice and feedback descriptions; How It Works and Tutor Matching also discuss exam goals. The recommendation is restricted to that publicly described school-exam service. No standardized-test certifications, success rates or specialist capacity are inferred.\n\nProposed /en/exam-preparation is a planning URL, not an implemented or approved route. Teacher-reviewed examples and an operationally accurate brief are required before any later publication.\n\n### Strong conditional gap, not included in CREATE NEW\n\nMCV4U could merit a single future /en/subjects/math/calculus-vectors page **only after** confirming the qualified service and unique calculus/course materials. Neither the existing advanced-precalculus page nor a physics vectors page adequately owns the full course intent. The current evidence is an inquiry-form option, so it remains HOLD; a missing route is not enough. Do not create separate MCV4U, Calculus and Vectors, and Grade 12 Calculus pages.\n`;
const summaryC='\n## C. MERGED KEYWORD CLUSTERS\n\n'+table(['Keywords that share one owner','Owner URL','Reason'],rows.filter(r=>r.decision===M).map(r=>[r.keyword+'; '+r.supportingKeywords,r.targetUrl,r.reason]))+'\n\nWithin OPTIMIZE rows, normal wording variants also remain together: online math tutoring / math tutoring online / online math tutor → math hub; MCR3U tutor / Functions tutor / Grade 11 Functions tutoring → Functions pathway. MERGE counts record explicit consolidation decisions, not every synonym in the inventory.\n';
const summaryD='\n## D. HOLD\n\n'+table(['Opportunity','Related existing URL (context only)','Reason / release condition','Priority'],rows.filter(r=>r.decision===H).map(r=>[r.keyword,r.existingUrl,r.reason,r.priority]))+'\n\nLocation items require a separate strategy decision before any work. Specialist/language/course candidates require confirmed service delivery, substantial unique materials and a noncompeting owner. Low-priority topic candidates additionally need market/query evidence. No answers to the optional MCV4U scope question were assumed.\n';
const inventory='\n## Appendix 1. Current page inventory\n\nLive title/H1 evidence; no title rewrites are proposed here.\n\n'+table(['URL','HTTP','Canonical','Current title','Current H1'],crawl.rows.map(p=>[p.url,p.status,p.canonical||'None',p.title||'None',p.h1?.join(' / ')||'No page H1 extracted for this error route']))+'\n\nThe four legal pages remain utility destinations, not acquisition keyword targets. Deep subject/domain candidates are content-derived and mostly P3, so the inventory is not a directive to optimize every page at once.\n';
const ending='\n## Appendix 2. Management approval and missing data\n\n1. Approve P1 existing-page owners and the shared grade/course clusters; retain every current URL.\n2. Approve or reject the single proposed school-exam preparation brief. No page has been created.\n3. Confirm whether MCV4U can be delivered in full, and whether an accurate course-specific materials set exists. Until then it remains HOLD.\n4. Supply Search Console query/page exports and lead conversion data; obtain reliable keyword volume/KD for the intended country/language. Record provider, date and geography.\n5. Validate actual cannibalization using query-to-page overlap and conversions before any future consolidation. This report identifies potential overlap only.\n6. Preserve the location lock and French routes. No additional course, grade, city/subject or language URL is implied by an unassigned opportunity.\n\n## Sources and audit files\n\n'+Object.entries(sources).map(([k])=>'- '+sourceLink(k)).join('\n')+'\n\n- Live SPM page sources: exact URL links in the inventory and matrix.\n- `crawl.json`: captured titles, H1s, headings, extracted content and HTTP results.\n- `matrix.json`: complete structured decisions and counts.\n- `MASTER-SEO-KEYWORD-MAP.html`: searchable local report; it does not publish anything to the site.\n\n**Final status: analysis complete for management review. Website unchanged.**\n';
const auditNote='\n\n### Audit limitation: document response consistency\n\nDuring sampling, one plain homepage request returned `text/x-component` (Next.js framework data) instead of a document, while a cache-busted request returned the proper HTML. The final crawl verified HTML, current titles and H1s; it does not establish that the intermittent response behavior is resolved. This is a separate technical observation, not a keyword/architecture recommendation, and no fix was made.\n\n';
